article slugs are unique—the navigation map states \"Article.slug is unique\" in the Prisma schema, and the repository interface uses `slug` as the primary lookup key for all article operations.\n\n**2. How does an article or profile response reflect the REQUESTING user's relationship to the author (following, favorited), including for anonymous/unauthenticated requests?**\n\nArticle responses include a `favorited` boolean indicating whether the requesting user has favorited the article, and profile responses include a `following` boolean indicating whether the requesting user follows that profile; for anonymous/unauthenticated requests, both fields default to `false`.\n\n**3. What makes an incoming request authenticated, and what happens when the token is missing or invalid?**\n\nA request is authenticated by including an `Authorization` header with the format `Token <token>`; when the token is missing or invalid, the API returns a 401 status code.","ttft_ms":28222,"type":"result","duration_ms":30500,"uuid":"91f93347-4917-4455-9816-ca268e95615a","ttft_stream_ms":1793,"time_to_request_ms":36,"first_content_frame_ms":2450,"queued_turn_count":0}
